# 基本図形編集: the desktop's own and the process write the same record (design 11.3),
# for tools/ui_run.py. Two copies of 画用紙 with 30 small rectangles (mkbig) are given
# the same changes, one in the desktop's figure editor (open) and one in the figure
# editor running as a process (pfig): the first rectangle carried 100 across and 200
# down, the third sized by its handle, the fifth thrown away, then saved. Record 0 of
# both must be the same, byte for byte.
# the desktop's figure editor opened by open, whatever the program object says (figproc kernel)
figproc kernel
mkbig fig 30 4
open big
waitwin 画用紙 600
sync 600
wait 500
click 111 128
drag 111 128 211 328
sync 600
click 135 128
wait 100
drag 143 136 183 166
sync 600
click 159 128
key 4C
sync 600
key 16 01
sync 600
shot cmp_kernel
sum
keep kernel
key 08 01
sync 600
wait 500
mkbig fig 30 4
logmark
pfig big
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 32
wait 500
logmark
click 111 128
drag 111 128 211 328
expectsince figure: moved 1 by 100,200
logmark
click 135 128
wait 100
drag 143 136 183 166
expectsince figure: sized
logmark
click 159 128
key 4C
expectsince figure: deleted, 31 shapes
logmark
key 16 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
shot cmp_process
sum
same kernel
key 08 01
expect figure: closed
